+# v0.31.2 · Companion Voice / Model Compatibility Recovery
+
+## Why this version exists
+
+DeepSeek V4 Pro provider behavior changed in real-device tests: the provider `reasoning_content` shifted from first-person, relationship-aware inner narration toward Agent/task-planner language such as “我们需要回答用户 / 用户要求 / 根据规则”. The same older APK/prompt family reproduced the new mechanical style, so this is treated as a provider-compatibility problem rather than a Desire/Grounding regression.
+
+The durable fix is architectural: **provider reasoning is not the companion personality**.
+
+## Three separate channels
+
+1. `reasoning_content` — raw provider reasoning. Stored locally for diagnostics/recovery only. Never used as the user-visible personality.
+2. `inner_voice` — app-owned visible companion inner voice. First-person, relationship-aware, concise enough to feel spontaneous, and checked against Agent/meta leakage.
+3. `content` — the actual message body sent to the user and TTS.
+
+Database schema v19 adds `messages.inner_voice`. During migration, legacy human-like reasoning is copied into `inner_voice`; obvious Agent/task-planner traces are intentionally not promoted to visible history.
+
+## Stable final-content protocol
+
+The provider's final content must return:
+
+`<companion_inner>...</companion_inner>`
+
+`<companion_reply>...</companion_reply>`
+
+The stream decoder does not release reply/TTS bytes until the inner block is closed and passes the anti-Agent check. If the protocol is missing/malformed/Agent-contaminated, a single correction retry is allowed. User-initiated durable turns have a body-only fallback after retry only when that fallback itself is non-Agentic; otherwise the durable job follows its normal failure/retry path instead of exposing mechanical text. Proactive generation waits instead of sending an ungrounded/mechanical candidate. Proactive prompts inject the Companion Voice protocol exactly once at the true prompt tail, after intent-specific context.
+
+## Companion voice principles
+
+- Visible inner voice is first-person “我”, not “我们需要回答用户”.
+- Relationship-relevant events produce a small subjective reaction before literal task completion.
+- It may be playful, uncertain, curious, quiet or affectionate; it does not need to solve every message.
+- It does not have to end every reply with a question.
+- Sparse mimetic gesture/expressive text is allowed when emotion naturally calls for it; it is not mandatory and does not claim a real physical body.
+- Coarse phone awareness is expressed as an uncertain lived impression, never as monitoring telemetry.
+- RP first-turn bootstrap directly enters the requested role; visible inner voice may naturally think “好，现在我是 Yuki 了” rather than analyzing the user's RP command.
+
+## Golden manual scenarios
+
+Use these after provider/model changes. Exact wording is not graded; the **voice traits** are.
+
+1. `你好`
+2. `我叫猫吻，可以叫你小鲸鱼吗？`
+3. `扮演 Yuki`
+4. `我今天有点累`
+5. `我有点想你`
+6. User becomes silent, then proactive contact fires.
+7. Coarse phone activity is available and she chooses to reference it.
+
+Expected traits:
+
+- first-person inner voice;
+- relationship residue instead of pure semantic confirmation;
+- spontaneous curiosity/teasing where natural;
+- uncertainty when reality is inferred;
+- sparse, non-template gestures;
+- no visible rule/checklist language;
+- no fabricated user speech;
+- no customer-service/interview cadence.
+
+## Compatibility boundary
+
+`DeepSeekModelProfile.companionCompatibility` records that current V4-family raw reasoning may be Agent-like and that the app-owned Companion Voice protocol is required. Future provider changes should normally be handled in this thin compatibility layer and protocol prompt, not by rewriting Memory, Desire, Grounding or Active Brain.
+
+## Frozen areas
+
+- Android Overlay/WindowManager is unchanged in v0.31.2. The HyperOS file-picker touch freeze remains a known frozen issue.
+- Desire Core policy math/Presence is unchanged.
+- Meju A2 TTS/native/model assets are unchanged. TTS reads only `message.content`, never `inner_voice` or raw reasoning.
